From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 13:24:15 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] gallium: preserve integer blit output types in NIR

Generated color blits already know their integer destination type. Carry it into NIR before driver finalization instead of losing it in the untyped TGSI output declaration. Preserve existing sample payloads and signedness clamps, and leave TGSI-only consumers, floating-point color, depth, and stencil paths unchanged.

Exercise all signedness pairs across sample, texel-fetch, and multisample paths, including backends that lower output IO during finalization.
